  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.2.7: Thread-safety fix for Piece (the per-piece block-download state machine). Piece is a 1:1 port of JS torrent-piece (single-threaded event loop); the C# client drives downloads from multiple threads, so the download loop's Reserve()/ReserveRemaining() could race a concurrent wire-arrival callback's Set()/Flush() (which null the piece buffers) → NullReferenceException on large multi-piece torrents (hit loading a 2.5GB SD-Turbo model). All Piece state mutators are now serialized on a per-Piece re-entrant lock (no-op on single-threaded WASM, atomic on desktop). v3.2.6: Adds TorrentFileInfo.ReadUint8ArrayAsync zero-copy JS-typed random-access read for browser GPU upload.",
